WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.530
A bony fish has no lungs.

2
00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:05.680
Water flows in through
its mouth, over the gills,

3
00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.970
and out under a bony flap.

4
00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:12.520
Float one gill arch in water, and
its fine filaments spread out.

5
00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:14.640
A locust has no lungs either.

6
00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:17.840
Just a row of tiny pores along its body.

7
00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:22.830
So how do fish and insects get
oxygen to their cells, without lungs?

8
00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:25.560
In this mission, you'll zoom into a gill,

9
00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:28.470
from the arch down to its thinnest plates.

10
00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:32.890
Then you'll find out where the air
goes once it is inside an insect.

11
00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:38.610
Your mission: explain how fish and insects
get oxygen to their cells without lungs.
